WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:09.000
<v Sara Khan>Thanks everyone. Quick retro on the Northwind onboarding project before we close it out.

2
00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:21.000
<v Sara Khan>Six weeks ago their onboarding took 41 days from signed contract to first live user. As of Friday it takes 6 days.

3
00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:36.000
<v Omar Ali>The biggest change wasn't the software. We deleted three steps nobody used: the kickoff deck, the security questionnaire re-review, and the second training call.

4
00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:50.000
<v Omar Ali>Honestly the questionnaire re-review alone was eleven days of waiting on legal for a document that never changed.

5
00:00:50.500 --> 00:01:04.000
<v Sara Khan>And the pricing stays confidential, but they renewed at 180k for next year, so please don't share that outside this room.

6
00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:18.000
<v Lina Park>What surprised me is that customers didn't miss the kickoff deck at all. Two of them said the first call felt faster and more useful without it.

7
00:01:18.500 --> 00:01:30.000
<v Sara Khan>Decision: we roll the 6-day onboarding out to every new customer starting next month. Omar owns the playbook, due the 15th.

8
00:01:30.500 --> 00:01:42.000
<v Lina Park>I'll update the help center articles by end of next week. Open question is whether enterprise customers will accept skipping the re-review.

9
00:01:42.500 --> 00:01:50.000
<v Sara Khan>"Remove before you automate" — that's the lesson I want the whole team to remember. Thanks all.
